    <string name="screen_time_calculation_method">Calculation method</string>
    <string name="screen_time_calculation_method_part_1_title">How is screen time calculated?</string>
    <string name="screen_time_calculation_method_part_1_details">The app calculates your screen time based on events related to opening and closing apps, as recorded by the Android system. Only the time spent using apps in the foreground is counted. Apps running in the background are not considered.</string>
    <string name="screen_time_calculation_method_part_2_title">Cases where screen time may not be counted</string>
    <string name="screen_time_calculation_method_part_2_details">- If the Android system does not record the event of opening or closing an app, the time spent during that session will not be counted.\n\n- If an app is uninstalled, the Android system deletes all events related to its use. Therefore, the screen time for that app will no longer be counted.</string>
    <string name="screen_time_calculation_method_part_3_title">How is screen time calculated when multiple apps are used in the foreground at the same time?</string>
    <string name="screen_time_calculation_method_part_3_details">When multiple apps are used in the foreground simultaneously (for example, in split-screen mode), the usage time for each app is counted separately.\n\nHowever, for the total screen time, only the actual time spent in front of the screen is counted, regardless of how many apps were active in the foreground at the same time.\n\nFor example, if two apps are used in the foreground simultaneously for 40 minutes, each app will show 40 minutes of usage, but the total screen time will remain 40 minutes, and not 80.</string>
